commit 6eaed78 — fix: unify experience encoding, correct skill input scale,
                 document IQR pre-CV methodology
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  src/neoai/features/build_features.py
    - Complete rewrite as single source of truth for all feature engineering
    - normalize_experience() covers all 14 actual dataset values:
        Fresher, 0-1, 0-2, 0-3, 02 Years, 03 Years,
        Fresher  1 Year, Fresher2 Years, Fresher  3 Years, etc.
    - Canonical labels: Fresher/Entry Level(0), 0-1 Years(1), 0-2 Years(2),
                        0-3 Years(3), Fresher-Mixed(3), Unknown(-1)
    - Added SKILL_INPUT_SCALE constant documenting 1-10 integer scale
    - CompanyFrequencyEncoder and SkillScaler moved here from cross_val scripts
    - add_static_features() is the single entry point for all pipeline stages

  src/neoai/models/cross_val_score_zero_outliers.py
    - Removed ~120 lines of local feature engineering functions
    - Now imports add_static_features, normalize_experience,
      EXPERIENCE_ENCODING, group_role from build_features

  src/neoai/models/cross_val_score.py
    - Removed local FinalFeatureSelector, group_role, normalize_experience,
      add_static_features definitions
    - Now imports from build_features

  src/neoai/models/predict_salary.py
    - Updated import to use add_static_features from build_features
    - Smoke test skill values corrected to realistic 1-10 scale
      (Python=7, Linux=8, AWS=7, Docker=7, Communication=8, etc.)
    - Docstring documents accepted Experience strings and 1-10 skill scale

  src/neoai/data/remove_salary_outliers.py
    - Added detailed methodology note to docstring explaining pre-CV IQR
      trade-off, impact (<1% bound shift), and future fix path (TransformerMixin)

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
