                             Windows Application Control policy
  mlflow           3.16.1    Installed version; pinned for reproducibility


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
8. KEY INSIGHTS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  - Actual dataset Experience values are all entry-level variants (Fresher,
    0-1, 0-2, 0-3 and typo variants). There are NO 1-2 Years, 2-4 Years,
    3-5 Years, 5-8 Years, 8+ Years values. The old encoding was entirely wrong.

  - Skill columns in training data are 1-10 integers (min=1, max=10,
    mean ~5-8). Using 0/1 binary values at prediction time produces z-scores
    below the training distribution minimum.

  - IQR outlier removal is applied to the full dataset before CV folds are
    created. This is a known methodology trade-off documented in
    remove_salary_outliers.py. Impact is small (<1% bound shift per fold).

  - Baseline train scripts (train_salary.py, train_salary_zero_outliers.py)
    use only 7 features (role group dummies + Experience_Encoded). The final
    model CV pipeline uses 18 features. These are intentionally different flows.
    The baseline models are NOT used for final prediction.

  - final_salary_model.pkl is a byte-for-byte copy of
    best_salary_model_zero_outliers_cv.pkl, generated by save_final_model.py
    via shutil.copy2.

  - Remote: https://dagshub.com/siddheshRajendraNimbalkar/NeoAI1stPipeline.git
    Branch: main
